WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
Model storage should balance control with startup performance.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:07.300
A managed repository can hold approved model versions, checksums, licenses,

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.835
and configuration metadata.

00:00:08.835 --> 00:00:13.475
Workers can copy approved artifacts into local SSD caches so inference does not depend on

00:00:13.475 --> 00:00:15.400
sustained access to shared storage.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.600
Define cache size, eviction policy,

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.385
and how a worker verifies that its local copy matches the version advertised to the

00:00:21.385 --> 00:00:21.900
router.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.800
Use explicit version identifiers rather than a mutable label such as latest.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.135
Model weights, quantization, tokenizer, prompt template, runtime,

00:00:29.135 --> 00:00:31.649
and serving parameters together influence behavior.

00:00:31.649 --> 00:00:35.875
Record that combination so results can be reproduced and a problematic release can be

00:00:35.875 --> 00:00:36.500
rolled back.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.500
Stage model changes on limited capacity, run representative evaluations,

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.600
and promote only after functional and performance checks pass.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.365
Separate model artifacts from private operational data.

00:00:46.365 --> 00:00:49.850
Prompts, outputs, uploaded files, embeddings, vector indexes,

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:53.695
and logs can contain sensitive information even when the model weights are public.

00:00:53.695 --> 00:00:56.620
Apply access controls, retention schedules, encryption,

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:59.400
and backup policies according to data classification.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:03.575
Avoid placing private data in a broadly readable model share simply because every worker

00:01:03.575 --> 00:01:04.464
can access it.

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:09.200
Back up what cannot be recreated: configuration, routing policy, secrets references,

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.464
evaluation results, metadata, and authorized private datasets.

00:01:12.464 --> 00:01:16.600
Large public model files may be restored from trusted sources if their exact versions and

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:17.800
hashes are recorded.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:22.105
Test restoration rather than equating a completed backup job with recoverability.

00:01:22.105 --> 00:01:26.295
Storage design succeeds when a new or recovered node can obtain the right model safely,

00:01:26.295 --> 00:01:29.500
start predictably, and avoid exposing unrelated data.
